  "nodes": [
   {
    "id": "h4_00001",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     11
    ],
    "text": "[A1][/A1]NAME",
    "placeholders": {
     "A1": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_363_01\" id=\"tag_17_363_01\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     13
    ],
    "text": "munmap — unmap pages of memory",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00003",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[A2][/A2]SYNOPSIS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A2": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_363_02\" id=\"tag_17_363_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00004",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     17,
     1
    ],
    "text": "[CODE3]",
    "placeholders": {
     "CODE3": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<code><tt>#include &lt;<a href=\"../basedefs/sys_mman.h.html\">sys/mman.h</a>&gt;<br>\n<br>\nint munmap(void *</tt><i>addr</i><tt>, size_t</tt> <i>len</i><tt>);<br></tt></code>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00005",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[A4][/A4]DESCRIPTION",
    "placeholders": {
     "A4": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_363_03\" id=\"tag_17_363_03\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I5]munmap[/I5]() function shall remove any mappings for those entire pages containing any part of the address space of the\nprocess starting at [I6]addr[/I6] and continuing for [I7]len[/I7] bytes. Further references to these pages shall result in the\ngeneration of a SIGSEGV signal to the process. If there are no mappings in the specified address range, then [I8]munmap[/I8]() has no\neffect.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I6": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I7": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I8": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00007",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The implementation may require that [I9]addr[/I9] be a multiple of the page size as returned by [A10][I11]sysconf[/I11]()[/A10].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I9": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A10": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/sysconf.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I11": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00008",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "If a mapping to be removed was private, any modifications made in this address range shall be discarded.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00009",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[S12][[A13]ML|MLR[/A13]][/S12] [IMG14]\nAny memory locks (see [A15][I16]mlock[/I16]()[/A15] and [A17][I18]mlockall[/I18]()[/A17]) associated with this address range shall be removed, as if by an appropriate\ncall to [A19][I20]munlock[/I20]()[/A19]. [IMG21]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S12": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A13": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;ML&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG14": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "A15": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/mlock.html#\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I16": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A17": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/mlockall.html#\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I18": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A19": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/munlock.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I20": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG21": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00010",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "[S22][[A23]TYM[/A23]][/S22] [IMG24]\nIf a mapping removed from a typed memory object causes the corresponding address range of the memory pool to be inaccessible by any\nprocess in the system except through allocatable mappings (that is, mappings of typed memory objects opened with the\nPOSIX_TYPED_MEM_MAP_ALLOCATABLE flag), then that range of the memory pool shall become deallocated and may become available to\nsatisfy future typed memory allocation requests.",
    "placeholders": {
     "S22": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A23": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;TYM&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG24": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00011",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     11
    ],
    "text": "A mapping removed from a typed memory object opened with the POSIX_TYPED_MEM_MAP_ALLOCATABLE flag shall not affect in any way\nthe availability of that typed memory for allocation. [IMG25]",
    "placeholders": {
     "IMG25": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00012",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The behavior of this function is unspecified if the mapping was not established by a call to [A26][I27]mmap[/I27]()[/A26].",
    "placeholders": {
     "A26": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/mmap.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I27": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00013",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[A28][/A28]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A28": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_363_04\" id=\"tag_17_363_04\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00014",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     25,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Upon successful completion, [I29]munmap[/I29]() shall return 0; otherwise, it shall return -1 and set [I30]errno[/I30] to indicate the\nerror.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I29": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I30": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00015",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     27
    ],
    "text": "[A31][/A31]ERRORS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A31": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_363_05\" id=\"tag_17_363_05\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00016",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I32]munmap[/I32]() function shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I32": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00017",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EINVAL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00018",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Addresses in the range [[I33]addr[/I33],[I34]addr[/I34]+[I35]len[/I35]) are outside the valid range for the address space of a\nprocess.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I33": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I34": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I35": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00019",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     7
    ],
    "text": "[EINVAL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00020",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The [I36]len[/I36] argument is 0.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I36": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00021",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I37]munmap[/I37]() function may fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I37": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00022",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     7,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EINVAL]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00023",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     7,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I38]addr[/I38] argument is not a multiple of the page size as returned by [A39][I40]sysconf[/I40]()[/A39].",
    "placeholders": {
     "I38": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A39": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/sysconf.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I40": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00024",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     35
    ],
    "text": "[A41][/A41]EXAMPLES",
    "placeholders": {
     "A41": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_363_06\" id=\"tag_17_363_06\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
